§ `Nouns of the Attorney General Law`

§§ `Bodies`

-- Section 1 defines "the executive authority" as the Government and all components of the executive authority that are not incorporated, and "court"
-- as whoever holds judicial power, the High Court of Justice included.
-- lsh:13 | "בית משפט" – מי שנתונה בידו סמכות שפיטה, לרבות בית המשפט הגבוה לצדק;
-- lsh:16 | "הרשות המבצעת" – הממשלה וכל גורמי הרשות המבצעת שאינם מאוגדים;
DECLARE `A kind of body` IS ONE OF
    `the Government`
    `a minister`
    `the Minister of Justice`
    `a unit of the executive that is not incorporated`
    `an incorporated body`
    `a holder of judicial or quasi-judicial power`
    `a court`
    `the Knesset`
    `another body of the State outside the executive`

§§ `Answers`

-- Chapter B, ss 7 to 10.
DECLARE `Who presents the position of the executive authority` IS ONE OF
    `the Attorney General`
    `another lawyer whom the Government has chosen`

DECLARE `Who fixes the position of the executive authority` IS ONE OF
    `the Government, by a position it has determined`
    `the Attorney General, where the Government has determined none`

-- Section 10(a): the approval without which the Attorney General does not appear.  "the Minister" is defined in s 1 as the Minister of Justice.
DECLARE `A way the Attorney General's appearance may be approved` IS ONE OF
    `approval of the Government`
    `approval of a ministerial committee`
    `approval of the Minister of Justice`
    `approval given in another way the Government determined`
    `no approval`

-- Section 5(b).
DECLARE `A Knesset committee` IS ONE OF
    `the Constitution, Law and Justice Committee`
    `the Foreign Affairs and Defense Committee`

-- Section 15(c).
DECLARE `To whom the Attorney General gives an account` IS ONE OF
    `the Minister of Justice`
    `the Commissioner for Complaints against State Representatives in the Courts`

§§ `What a cross-reference is about`

-- The subject a provision has, by its own heading and text.  A cross-reference is checked by comparing the subject the CITING text says the target has with the subject the TARGET has.
DECLARE `A subject of a provision` IS ONE OF
    `definitions`
    `the exceptions to the binding force of an opinion`
    `the force of a written opinion on the existing law`
    `the Government's decision that an opinion need not be followed`
    `the position of the executive authority`
    `notice that the Attorney General cannot present the position`
    `presentation of the position by another lawyer`
    `the Attorney General's appearance`
    `the Attorney General's tasks in advising the Government`
    `the Attorney General's duty to present the position`
    `what Chapter B does not apply to`
    `Chapter B`
    `a power conferred by enactment on the Attorney General`
    `the Attorney General's independence in criminal-law matters`
    `the account the Attorney General gives the Minister`
    `representation of the State in a proceeding`
    `the Government's power over the appointment of the Attorney General`
    `the office that receives complaints about State representatives`
    `a committee of the Knesset`
    `the power to appear and be heard in a proceeding`

DECLARE `A reference the Law makes` HAS
    `where the reference is made`                            IS A STRING
    `what it cites`                                          IS A STRING
    `the subject the citing text says the target has`        IS A `A subject of a provision`
    `the subject the target has`                             IS A `A subject of a provision`
    `the target is in the Law or the cited instrument`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the target is in the Law itself`                        IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Readings`

-- Fork F3: how "within 30 days from the day of its commencement" (s 20) is counted.
DECLARE `A reading of how s 20 counts its 30 days` IS ONE OF
    `the commencement day is not counted`
    `the commencement day is counted as day one`
    `the count is declined`
